# Line endings of byte-exact inputs.
#
# Several checks compare these files byte-for-byte (the dataset hash lock datasets/calls/conversations.sha256, the committed evaluation package
# evaluation/semantic_annotation/, the protected-file hash comparisons in tests), and some CSV fields contain quoted multi-line text (every datasets/emails/emails.csv
# body), so a CRLF checkout (Windows with core.autocrlf=true) changes the DATA, not only the hash.  Pin them to LF in every checkout, whatever the local git
# configuration.  Source code, documentation and UI files are intentionally NOT listed: their line endings carry no meaning for any check.
*.csv    text eol=lf
*.jsonl  text eol=lf
*.sql    text eol=lf
datasets/**/*.json    text eol=lf
datasets/**/*.sha256  text eol=lf
data/**/*.json        text eol=lf
evaluation/**/*.json  text eol=lf
evaluation/**/*.md    text eol=lf

# Databases are binary: never convert (the seed databases are shipped test fixtures).
*.db       binary
*.sqlite   binary
*.sqlite3  binary
